This <University of Oxford> Part B paper covers Mathematical Ecology and Biology in section A and Nonlinear Systems in section B. It is cross-listed for Mathematics, Mathematics and Computer Science, and Mathematics and Statistics. https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/maths_past_papers_3[Source release]{ref} A bounded official-source search found no advertised answers for this exact paper. The complete archive transcription retains its supplied graph and printed map; the solutions include the antipodal <two-cycle> lost by the proposed quadratic reduction.

= A
